Root cause found for prior constructor segfault
- The previous constructor emission retried this round and reproduced the `--as-c` crash on:
  - `test/match_recursive_arg.hvm`
  - `test/use_match_depth.hvm`
- ASAN on host `clang/main` showed the crash was emitter-time stack overflow, not generated-runtime corruption:
  - deep recursion in `aot_emit_node` at constructor field recursion (`emit.c` old line ~499).
- Trigger: deep static constructor literals (e.g., `100000n`) cause huge recursive expansion if fields are emitted recursively.
- Fix: constructor fields are now lazily captured (non-recursive emission), which avoids emitter stack blowup.

